From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pengy <pengy@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kiumd: guard DEFINE_FREE(fput) already in linux/file.h

Kernel 7.x linux/file.h already defines DEFINE_FREE(fput).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [out-of-tree module compat fix]
Signed-off-by: Ajender Reddy Mallikarjuna <ajenderr@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 safelinux-modules/drivers/kiumd.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/safelinux-modules/drivers/kiumd.c b/safelinux-modules/drivers/kiumd.c
--- a/safelinux-modules/drivers/kiumd.c
+++ b/safelinux-modules/drivers/kiumd.c
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@
  */
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 0)
 DEFINE_FREE(fput, struct file *, if (_T) fput(_T))
+#endif
 
 /**
